{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And they shall live.</b> They will add life." "<b>And they shall not die.</b> By excision. The meaning is that if they keep [the command] they will receive reward, and if not, they will be punished, for it is possible that they would not be punished — therefore, 'and they shall not die.'" "<b>And they shall set them.</b> The ark and the table and the lampstand and the altars." "<b>For its service.</b> With the holy vessels." "<b>And to its burden.</b> To carry on the shoulder."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:18.066987594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}